course: dictionary
lesson: 5235
title: Jew: a name for a people and a faith
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A Jew is a person whose religion is Judaism, or who belongs to the Jewish people by family and culture. Read the context to find the clues. «The Sabbath is a day of rest and worship; most Christians keep Sunday, and Jews keep Saturday.» So Jews are people who keep a special day of rest and worship on Saturday.
explain: Jew is a noun, so you can say a Jew or Jews. It is a name for a people and a faith, so it starts with a capital J, just as Christian and Muslim do. A name for a faith or a people is always written with a capital letter.
explain: Always use Jew and Jewish with respect. In history, the word names real people who were treated cruelly, so never use it as an insult or a joke.
fact: A Jew is a person whose religion is Judaism, or who belongs to the Jewish people by family and culture.
fact: Jew is written with a capital J because it names a people and a faith.
fact: Jews worship in a synagogue, and they keep Shabbat, a day of rest and worship.
fact: In history, we learn that «the Nazis murdered about six million Jews, as well as many Roma, disabled people and others, only because of who they were; this is called the Holocaust.»
exercise: «Jews keep Saturday as their day of rest and worship.» Which day do Jews keep? | Sunday | Monday | Wednesday | *Saturday
exercise: Which spelling is correct for the name of a people and a faith? | jew | *Jew | jews, all in small letters | JEW in capitals
exercise: Where do Jews worship? | A football ground | A castle | *A synagogue | A church
test: A Jew is a person whose religion is Judaism, or who belongs to the Jewish people by family and culture. What is a Jew? | Any person who lives in Germany | A kind of festival | A town in Germany | *A person of the Jewish faith or people
test: «The Nazis murdered about six million Jews, only because of who they were.» What does this tell us? | It was a happy festival | Jews chose to leave Germany | *People were killed because of who they were | Six million people won a prize
exam: Which sentence uses the word Jew correctly? | many jews keep shabbat | Jew is a day of the week | The jew went to the synagogue on Monday | *Many Jews keep Shabbat, their day of rest and worship
